        "evidence": "The new ManagementAuthorityId is deployment-owned, included in digest v2 and persisted with the batch. Existing-batch read-only binding compares target, organizational membership, root bindings and context references while allowing the fresh grant's current advisory-content digest to differ, but it does not require the current grant's ManagementAuthorityId to equal the batch's stored authority ID. A different management deployment with colliding Repository and context record IDs could therefore bind historical context selected under the previous authority.",
